From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:47:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wpa_supplicant: associate with the known links when the ML probe scan cannot start

wpa_supplicant_connect_ml_missing() requests an ML probe scan before
the association with an AP MLD whose affiliated links are missing from
the scan results. That scan is a manual scan request, and
wpas_trigger_scan_cb() does not retry a manual scan that the driver
refuses. The station then stays in SCANNING, and nothing requests
another scan while it is not connected. A radio that several
interfaces share refuses the scan with EBUSY while another interface
scans on it, for example an AP in ACS right after a radio restart.

Associate with the links that the scan results describe when the ML
probe scan cannot start, as after an ML probe request that the AP MLD
does not answer. The links that stay missing are left out of the
association.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 wpa_supplicant/events.c           |    2 +-
 wpa_supplicant/scan.c             |    7 +++++++
 wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant_i.h |    1 +
 3 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/wpa_supplicant/events.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/events.c
@@ -1924,7 +1924,7 @@ static void wpa_supplicant_scan_abort_re
 }


-static bool ml_link_probe_scan(struct wpa_supplicant *wpa_s)
+bool ml_link_probe_scan(struct wpa_supplicant *wpa_s)
 {
 	if (!wpa_s->ml_connect_probe_ssid || !wpa_s->ml_connect_probe_bss)
 		return false;
--- a/wpa_supplicant/scan.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/scan.c
@@ -267,6 +267,13 @@ static void wpas_trigger_scan_cb(struct
 			/* Restore scan_req since we will try to scan again */
 			wpa_s->scan_req = wpa_s->last_scan_req;
 			wpa_supplicant_req_scan(wpa_s, 1, 0);
+		} else if (!wpa_s->disconnected && ml_link_probe_scan(wpa_s)) {
+			/*
+			 * The ML probe request could not be sent, so the
+			 * association proceeds with the links that the scan
+			 * results already describe, as after an ML probe
+			 * request that the AP MLD did not answer.
+			 */
 		} else if (wpa_s->scan_res_handler) {
 			/* Clear the scan_res_handler */
 			wpa_s->scan_res_handler = NULL;
--- a/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant_i.h
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant_i.h
@@ -2032,6 +2032,7 @@ void wpa_supplicant_mark_disassoc(struct
 int wpa_supplicant_connect(struct wpa_supplicant *wpa_s,
 			   struct wpa_bss *selected,
 			   struct wpa_ssid *ssid);
+bool ml_link_probe_scan(struct wpa_supplicant *wpa_s);
 void wpa_supplicant_stop_countermeasures(void *eloop_ctx, void *sock_ctx);
 void wpa_supplicant_delayed_mic_error_report(void *eloop_ctx, void *sock_ctx);
 void wnm_bss_keep_alive_deinit(struct wpa_supplicant *wpa_s);
